The '''climate of [[Agra]]''' features a [[semi-arid climate]] that borders on a [[humid subtropical climate]]. The city features mild winters, hot and dry summers and a monsoon season. The [[monsoon]], though substantial in Agra, is not quite as heavy as the monsoon in other parts of India. The mean annual rainfall of Agra district is {{cvt|671|mm}}.<ref name="Gardner_2024">{{cite journal |last1=Gardner |first1=Bob Stanley |last2=Durjoy Lal Soren |first2=David |last3=Lois Chauhan |first3=Nelia |last4=Biswas |first4=Brototi |last5=Gardner |first5=Shalomin |title=Unveiling Climatic Trends from 1922 to 2022: A Long-Term Time-Series Analysis of Precipitation of Semi-Arid Agra District, Uttar Pradesh, India |journal=Geography and Regional Future Studies |date=22 August 2024 |volume=2 |issue=2 |pages=78–84 |doi=10.30466/grfs.2024.55117.1046 }}</ref> The district receives the majority of this rainfall during the monsoon months i.e., June to September, which averages around {{cvt|603|mm}}.<ref name="Gardner_2024"/> Agra has a reputation for being one of the hottest and the coldest towns in India. In summer the city witnesses a sudden surge in temperature and at times, mercury goes beyond the {{cvt|46|°C}} mark in addition to a very high level of humidity. During summer, the daytime temperature hovers around {{cvt|46|-|50|°C}}. Nights are relatively cooler and temperature lowers to {{cvt|30|°C}}. Winter minimum temperatures sometimes go as low as {{cvt|3|or|3.5|°C}} but usually hover in the range of {{cvt|6|-|8|°C}}.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bharatonline.com/uttar-pradesh/travel/agra/weather.html |title=Agra Weather |website=Bharat Online}}</ref>

==Factors==
The [[monsoon]] and the [[Western Disturbance]] are the two main factors that alter the weather over Agra; otherwise, Continental air will prevail for the rest of the year. Like most cities of Northwestern India, the weather and climate of Agra are extreme and [[subtropical]] in nature. The following are the main factors that influence the weather in Agra:

*Western Disturbances mostly occur during the winter months and cause light to moderate showers, temperature also decreases due to it.
*Southwest Monsoon occurs in summer from June till September. Monsoon rains bring much-awaited relief from the scorching heat. These monsoon rains are quite heavy by nature and can cause significant flooding.
*Continental air prevails during the period when there is no precipitation in Agra.

==Monthly weather conditions==
Like other cities, Agra has four seasons: winter (Dec-Feb), summer (May-Sept), autumn (Oct-Nov) and spring (March–April). The monsoon season occurs in the summer. The following is a monthly summary of climatic conditions in Agra based on data from the [[India Meteorological Department]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.imd.gov.in/section/nhac/mean/AGRA.htm |title=Archived copy |accessdate=2010-12-16 |url-status=dead |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20101224230229/http://imd.gov.in/section/nhac/mean/AGRA.htm |archivedate=2010-12-24 }}</ref>

===January===
January is the coldest month in the city and [[Western Disturbance]] also occurs in this month coming from Northern [[Pakistan]]. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|26.1|C|F}} in 1932. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|3.1|C|F}} in 1927 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|51.8|mm|in}} in 1947.

===February===
Cold conditions continue until the middle of February, after that the weather becomes settled and pleasant. Winter showers also occur in this month. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|29.1|C|F}} in 1993. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|5.8|C|F}} in 1925 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|506.2|mm|in}} in 1980.

===March===
Hot and dry weather returns during March. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|35.4|C|F}} in 1994. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|10.7|C|F}} in 2000 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|45.7|mm|in}} in 1944.

===April===
Temperatures start to rise in this month. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|41.1|C|F}} in 1921. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|16.4|C|F}} in 1999 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|61.8|mm|in}} in 1984.

===May===
May is the hottest month of Agra city. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|44.6|C|F}} in 1921. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|18.6|C|F}} in 1999 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|62.0|mm|in}} in 1987.
[[File:Taj Mahal through the early morning mist, Agra.jpg|thumb|300px|left|Mist surrounds the Taj Mahal]]

===June===
It remains hot but during the middle or end of June, pre-monsoon showers can start. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|43.3|C|F}} in 1924. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|17.5|C|F}} in 1999 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|355.8|mm|in}} in "1952".

===July===
Monsoon season starts in July. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|40.7|C|F}} in 1911. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|19.6|C|F}} in 2000 and highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|551.2|mm|in}} in 1994.

===August===
August is the wettest month of Agra city. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|37.4|C|F}} in 1987. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|16.7|C|F}} in 1999 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|617.7|mm|in}} in 1957.

===September===
The intensity of rainstorm decreases in the month of September as monsoon starts to withdraw. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|38.4|C|F}} in 1913. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|17.1|C|F}} in 1999 and highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|609.0|mm|in}} in 1939.

===October===
Post-monsoon rains could occur in this month. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|36.1|C|F}} in 1993. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|14.6|C|F}} in 1999 and the Highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|268.7|mm|in}} in 1911.

===November===
It is the driest month of the city. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|30.7|C|F}} in 1987. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|8.0|C|F}} in 1999 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|75.9|mm|in}} in 1969.

===December===
Winter season begins in this month. The highest monthly average maximum temperature recorded was {{convert|25.8|C|F}} in 1992. The lowest monthly average minimum temperature recorded was {{convert|3.7|C|F}} in 1999 and the highest monthly rainfall recorded was {{convert|62.6|mm|in}} in 1967.

